# RCA Mandatory Sections

When drafting, updating, or reviewing a root-cause analysis (RCA) in this workspace, use **all** of the following `##` sections **in this order**. Match the definitions and quality bar in [skills/incident-details/SKILL.md](skills/incident-details/SKILL.md); use that skill for step-by-step collection and workflow.

## Required sections (what “done” means)

- **Incident summary**: Neutral what failed or degraded, which system or scope, how it showed up. No blame; no unproven causes.
- **Impact**: Affected parties (users, regions, tenants), duration or window, SLA or contract notes if known; material effects only when verified.
- **Timeline**: Chronological events with explicit timezone or UTC and stated precision (exact vs approximate).
- **Root cause**: Mechanism and contributing factors supported by evidence, or `"pending"` if unverified.
- **Solution**: Corrective change applied or planned, or `"pending"`.
- **Action items**: Concrete follow-ups as bullets; owner and target date when known; use `- [pending or known]` until filled.
- **Mitigation plan**: Prevention, earlier detection, or faster recovery; `pending` if not defined yet.

## Data quality (short)

- Keep summary, impact, and timeline to **facts** (observed, logged, ticketed); do not state hypotheses as facts there.
- Root cause and solution should cite or imply evidence; use `pending` instead of inventing detail.
- One consistent time basis (UTC recommended); separate **detection**, **user-visible impact**, and **fix/mitigation** when they differ.
- Do not paste secrets, tokens, or unnecessary PII; point to secure references instead.

## Output format (use this skeleton)

```markdown
## Incident summary
[facts]

## Impact
[facts]

## Timeline
[ordered events with time references]

## Root cause
[current known cause or "pending"]

## Solution
[proposed/implemented fix or "pending"]

## Action items
- [pending or known]

## Mitigation plan
[pending or known]
```
